Final answer: ### 1. Task outcome (short version):
Screened 23 studies for inclusion in a systematic review on menopausal status, ultrasound, and biomarker tests for 
ovarian cancer diagnosis. Applied selection criteria focusing on cross-sectional diagnostic test accuracy studies, RCTs,
or multivariable model validation studies evaluating test combinations with histological/clinical follow-up reference 
standard in women with suspicious pelvic masses. Final decisions: 21 INCLUDE, 2 EXCLUDE.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
I systematically evaluated each of the 23 studies in the chunk against the review's selection criteria. The criteria 
required: (1) study design being either cross-sectional diagnostic test accuracy (evaluating single tests or comparing 
≥2 tests), RCT comparing ≥2 tests, or study validating a multivariable model for test combinations; (2) reference 
standard of histological confirmation or clinical follow-up; (3) population of women with pelvic mass (clinically or 
USS-detected) suspicious for ovarian cancer. I applied a conservative approach (include when uncertain) and wrote 
study-specific rationales.

Included studies (21):
1. Study 1: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Evaluates HE4, CA125, ROMA, RMI as diagnostic tools; diagnostic accuracy study
comparing multiple biomarkers; population: pelvic mass patients; reference standard unclear from abstract but study 
evaluates diagnostic performance suggesting histology follow-up.
2. Study 2: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Prospective cross-sectional study assessing HE4, CA125, ROMA for ovarian cancer 
vs. endometriosis differentiation; reference standard: final pathologic results (histology); population: women with 
pelvic mass.
3. Study 3: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Retrospective diagnostic accuracy study validating the IOTA ADNEX model 
(multivariable model) for adnexal masses; reference standard: histology; population: women with adnexal mass.
4. Study 4: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Retrospective case note audit on CA125 usage patterns; evaluates diagnostic 
performance of CA125 for ovarian cancer suspicion; reference standard: clinical follow-up via case notes; population: 
patients with CA125 measurements.
5. Study 5: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Retrospective diagnostic accuracy study externally validating the ADNEX model 
(multivariable model) and comparing with other ultrasound methods; reference standard: pathology (histology); 
population: women with adnexal pathology.
6. Study 6: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Systematic review and meta-analysis comparing ROMA and RMI-I (test 
combinations) for ovarian cancer diagnosis; evaluates diagnostic accuracy of test combinations; population: women with 
adnexal mass; reference standard unclear but implies histology from included studies.
7. Study 7: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Study evaluating RMI variants (test combinations) for ovarian malignancy 
prediction; reference standard: histology; population: women with adnexal masses.
8. Study 8: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Prospective multicenter study comparing HE4, CA125, ROMA diagnostic accuracy 
(test combinations); evaluates diagnostic performance of biomarker combinations; population: Chinese women with 
epithelial ovarian cancer; reference standard unclear but implies histology.
9. Study 9: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Study evaluating HE4 vs. CA125 vs. ROMA (test combinations) in benign/malignant 
gynecological diseases; reference standard: histology; population: women with gynecological diseases including ovarian 
cancer.
10. Study 10: EXCLUDE (medium confidence) - Systematic review on symptoms associated with ovarian cancer diagnosis; not 
a diagnostic test accuracy study evaluating test performance/combinations; lacks test evaluation component.
11. Study 11: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Systematic review and meta-analysis comparing HE4, CA125, ROMA as markers 
(test combinations) for ovarian cancer; evaluates diagnostic accuracy of biomarker combinations; population: ovarian 
cancer patients and healthy individuals; reference standard unclear but implies histology.
12. Study 12: EXCLUDE (medium confidence) - Global cancer statistics epidemiology study; not a diagnostic test accuracy 
study for ovarian cancer; lacks diagnostic evaluation and target population focus.
13. Study 13: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Prospective multicenter diagnostic study validating the ADNEX model 
(multivariable model) for ovarian cancer staging; reference standard: histology/surgical staging; population: women with
ovarian mass.
14. Study 14: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Retrospective study comparing CA-125, HE4, RMI-II, ROMA (test combinations) in
pelvic mass differential diagnosis; reference standard: histology; population: women with adnexal neoplasia.
15. Study 15: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Prospective case-control study evaluating HE4+CA125 combination for ovarian 
cancer detection; evaluates diagnostic accuracy of biomarker combination; population: women with adnexal mass and 
healthy controls; reference standard unclear but implies histology.
16. Study 16: INCLUDE (medium confidence) - Study evaluating HE4 and ROMA as diagnostic/prognostic tools for epithelial 
ovarian cancer; evaluates diagnostic performance of biomarkers; population: women with ovarian cysts, endometriosis, 
benign cysts, EOC; reference standard unclear but implies histology.
17. Study 17: INCLUDE (high confidence) - Prospective multicenter diagnostic accuracy study comparing IOTA strategies 
