also conducted to update and supplement the evidentiary base. A bivariate, random-effects meta-regression model was used
to produce summary estimates of sensitivity and specificity and to plot summary ROC curves with 95% confidence regions. 
RESULTS Four meta-analyses and 53 primary studies were included in this review. The diagnostic performance of each 
technology was compared and contrasted based on the summary data on sensitivity and specificity obtained from the 
meta-analysis. Results suggest that 3D ultrasonography has both a higher sensitivity and specificity when compared to 2D
ultrasound. Established morphological scoring systems also performed with respectable sensitivity and specificity, each 
with equivalent diagnostic competence. Explicit scoring systems did not perform as well as other diagnostic testing 
