{\"study_index\": 63, \"title\": \"HE4 and CA125 as a diagnostic test in ovarian cancer: prospective validation of the  
Risk of Ovarian Malignancy Algorithm\", \"abstract\": \"BACKGROUND Recently, a Risk of Ovarian Malignancy Algorithm     
(ROMA) utilising human epididymis secretory protein 4 (HE4) and CA125 successfully classified patients as presenting a  
high or low risk for epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC). We validated this algorithm in an independent prospective study.  
METHODS Women with a pelvic mass, who were scheduled to have surgery, were enrolled in a prospective study. Preoperative
